# Commands run by the launchd job com.hakios.demo (see com.hakios.demo.plist).
# The default rc.jobs, and then two more ps snapshots a minute apart: the first
# one runs nine seconds into the boot, before lsd has even been spawned, and the
# process that fills the console with "denied attempt to escape CPU monitor" is
# measured nowhere. TIME is cumulative, so two snapshots say who is spending the
# CPU while the phone gets warm (notes/remaining-hardware.md, 2026-11-05).
/redwood/bin/hello_dyn started by launchd
/redwood/bin/svc_test
/redwood/bin/surf_test
/bin/ps -A
/redwood/bin/mg_test
# the processors: how many, and -- once the system has settled -- whether they work at the same time
/redwood/bin/cpu_test
/redwood/bin/cpu_test 240 &
# lsd is spawned about eight seconds in; these snapshots bracket the minute
# in which the GPU frames are drawn and the CPU monitor complains about lsd.
# Twenty seconds apart: with thirty the last one lands after the kernel has
# begun to come back and never prints (020310, 90 s round). For a 150 s round
# all five print; the point is whether lsd's TIME stops growing once the
# LaunchServices database and the containers are built.
sleep 20
/bin/ps -A
sleep 20
/bin/ps -A
sleep 20
/bin/ps -A
sleep 20
/bin/ps -A
sleep 20
/bin/ps -A
